+    {lvl:"Level 3",name:"Channel Divinity: Weigh the Futures",body:"<p>As a {{magicaction}} and a use of {{channeldivinity}}, choose a creature you can see within 60 feet. It makes a Wisdom {{savingthrow|saving throw}}. On a failure, you show it two futures, and at the start of its next turn it must choose one:</p><p><b>Stand Still.</b> Its {{speed|Speed}} is 0 until the end of that turn.</p><p><b>Lose the Moment.</b> It can't take actions or Bonus Actions until the end of that turn.</p><p>On a success, nothing happens.</p>"},
+    {lvl:"Level 6",name:"The Unchosen Future",body:"<p>When a creature chooses a future from Weigh the Futures, choose up to a number of other creatures equal to your {{proficiencybonus|Proficiency Bonus}} that you can see within 30 feet of it, and roll a d6 for each one. On a 1–3, the future passes it by. On a 4 or 5, it must make a Wisdom {{savingthrow|saving throw}} against your spell save DC at the start of its next turn. On a 6, it makes that save twice, once for each future.</p><p>On a failed save, the creature suffers the future in full. On a success, it suffers a half version. <b>Stand Still, halved:</b> its Speed is halved until the end of its turn. <b>Lose the Moment, halved:</b> it can take an action or a Bonus Action that turn, but not both.</p><p><b>Reflected Die.</b> After you roll, you can reflect one die so it shows the opposite face (7 minus the roll). You can do this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a {{longrest|Long Rest}}.</p>"},
+    {lvl:"Level 17",name:"Hall of Reflections",body:"<p>Once per {{longrest|Long Rest}}, as a {{magicaction}}, choose up to a number of creatures equal to your {{proficiencybonus|Proficiency Bonus}} that you can see within 60 feet. A willing creature needs no save. Any other creature makes a Wisdom {{savingthrow|saving throw}}, and a successful save leaves it unaffected. Each affected creature becomes {{reflected|Reflected}} for 1 minute.</p><p>Whenever a Reflected creature makes a {{d20test|D20 Test}}, you can reflect the roll. This takes no action, and you can do it once per round per Reflected creature, after the roll and before the outcome is known. The d20 shows the opposite face, so the result becomes 21 minus the roll. A natural 1 becomes a natural 20, and a natural 20 becomes a natural 1.</p><p>When you reflect a natural 1 or a natural 20, you regain one expended use of Reflected Die.</p>"}
+  ]};
